  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "I like doing something",
     "texto": [
      "With **любить** + infinitive: **Я люблю читать** (I like reading), **я люблю гулять** (I like going for walks), **я люблю путешествовать** (I like travelling).",
      "**Что ты любишь делать в свободное время?** = what do you like doing in your free time? **Свободное время** is «free time»."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Playing and playing an instrument: играть",
     "texto": [
      "In Russian it is the same verb, **играть** (играю, играешь, играет), but the preposition and the form of the noun change.",
      "Sports and games, with **в + accusative**: играть **в футбол**, **в теннис**, **в шахматы** (chess).",
      "Instruments, with **на + prepositional**: играть **на гитаре** (to play the guitar; гитара → гитаре)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Going often: ходить",
     "texto": [
      "To talk about an activity or a destination you go to **regularly or repeatedly**, **ходить** is used: хожу, ходишь, ходит. It does not necessarily mean going on foot: **ходить в спортзал** usually means «to go to the gym».",
      "**Я часто хожу в кино** = I often go to the cinema. **Я хожу в спортзал каждый день** = I go to the gym every day.",
      "**Идти** usually describes a specific journey in one direction, in progress or planned; **ходить** expresses regular, repeated movement or back-and-forth movement. **Гулять** means to go for a walk or a stroll."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
